*6(b) Display lines b/w start and end line numbers using shell script passed as argument*

*Steps:*
1) Open terminal
2) Create the script -> nano http://exp6b.sh
3) Enter:
#!/bin/bash
read -p "Enter filename: " file
read -p "Enter starting line number: " start
read -p "Enter ending line: " end
sed -n "${start},${end}p" "$file"
4) Save using Ctrl+O -> Enter and exit using Ctrl+X
5) Give Execution permission -> chmod +x http://exp6b.sh
6) Create a sample file -> nano http://test.txt Enter several lines Save and Exit
7) Run the script -> ./exp6b.sh
8) Enter the filename, starting line and ending line when asked

*Result:* The specified range of lines is displayed from the file
